Description: End comments as the HTML tokenizer does
 A comment ends at two or more dashes before ">", the extra dashes being
 part of its text, and at "--!>". "<!-->" and "<!--->" are empty comments.
 Upstream only ended a comment at exactly "-->", so each of these left the
 comment open and took in the rest of the file.
Author: Numiko
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: no
Test: test/parser/parse-for-eslint.test.ts ("markup read as a browser reads it")
Last-Update: 2026-11-04
